[[File:Iego_system.jpg|thumb|right|300px|The moons of Iego]]
{{Quote|Are you an angel? [&hellip;] I've heard the deep space pilots talk about them. They're the most beautiful creatures in the universe. They live on the moons of Iego, I think.|Anakin Skywalker, to Padmé Amidala|audio=AreYouAnAngel-TPM.flac|<ref name="The Phantom Menace">{{Film|I}}</ref>}}
The '''moons of Iego'''<ref name="The Phantom Menace" /> were a group of a thousand [[moon]]s that surrounded the [[planet]] [[Iego]],<ref name="Mystery of a Thousand Moons">{{TCW|Mystery of a Thousand Moons}}</ref> each as mysterious as the planet itself. The largest of the moons was [[Millius Prime]], the [[homeworld]] of the mysterious [[Diathim]]. Other moons included [[Clepresdan]], [[Flitrude]], [[Winlion]], [[Rawnde]], [[Cobarb]], and [[Uncovalor]].<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> During the [[High Republic Era]], [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Wes Vinik]] chased a gang of [[pirates]], who had stolen a [[Republic]] [[starship]], through the moons.<ref name="Heroes and Hotshots">{{YJA|Heroes and Hotshots}}</ref>

{{Moon-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The moons of Iego were first mentioned in the [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']]<ref name="The Phantom Menace" /> and first appeared in "[[Mystery of a Thousand Moons]]," the eighteenth episode of the [[canon]] animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''{{'}} [[The Clone Wars: Season One|first season]],<ref name="Mystery of a Thousand Moons" /> which originally aired on [[February 13]], [[2009]].<ref name="Mystery of a Thousand Moons air date">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode018.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Mystery of a Thousand Moons}}</ref>

